    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "START HERE \u00b7 full workflow",
      "pos": [
        60,
        30
      ],
      "size": [
        1230,
        370
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 19,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Choose one source: Performance Capture, Swing Choreo, or Load motion.\n2. For existing local results, open Load Motion \u2192 Saved jobs, refresh, and select a job. No Cartwheel connection is needed for saved or uploaded files.\n3. Keep PREVIEW OR GENERATE on Preview camera and Run. Edit the camera, then Run again to update/save it.\n4. Add optional creative references, choose Seedance/H3, then select Generate final video when ready.\nEvery completed camera preview saves a local job. Retain the saved files in your ComfyUI output directory for reuse or Blender."
      ],
      "color": "#263749",
      "bgcolor": "#17232f"
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "SOURCE SELECTION \u00b7 one dropdown",
      "pos": [
        60,
        2450
      ],
      "size": [
        1230,
        370
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 20,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Choose Performance Capture, Swing Choreo or Load motion. Only the selected source runs.\nLoad motion offers Upload files and Saved jobs. Saved jobs reads this ComfyUI output folder without contacting Cartwheel. Existing local captures also appear there.\nRun Camera Preview to save a reusable local job, including actors, original camera, edited camera samples/settings and a preview. Retained job files are in your ComfyUI output directory.\nFor new paid jobs, select Performance Capture or Swing Choreo explicitly."
      ],
      "color": "#263749",
      "bgcolor": "#17232f"
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "REFERENCES + TRIMMING \u00b7 optional inputs are prewired",
      "pos": [
        2720,
        30
      ],
      "size": [
        930,
        440
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 21,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "CREATIVE REFERENCES\nAdd multiple images, videos and audio in the Reference Library below. Uncheck an entry to omit it without removing the file. Enabled files are numbered in list order; the edited camera render is Video 1 when enabled. Describe their roles in your prompt.\nSeedance 2.5: up to 30 images, 10 videos, 10 audios. H3: up to 9 images, 3 videos, 3 audios. Counts include the camera video. Video references share 30s (Seedance) / 15s (H3); audio has a separate shared allowance. Automatic windows split the budget. Each video/audio needs at least 1.8s. Native provider validation also applies.\nPrepare never submits a job. Generate uses the selected model\u2019s built-in ComfyUI API node. Ratio remains adaptive."
      ],
      "color": "#263749",
      "bgcolor": "#17232f"
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "OUTPUTS \u00b7 save and compare",
      "pos": [
        4170,
        530
      ],
      "size": [
        580,
        230
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 22,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "PREVIEW FIRST\nPreview camera renders and saves the edited camera video without requesting either video model or loading the creative references.\nAfter editing, choose Generate final video and Run. Only the selected model is submitted.\nSave edited camera retains your full control render. Result video saves the model output. Comparison saves the selected control window beside the generated result, starting together and holding the shorter side at its last frame. Comparison is silent.\nThe action remains selected until you change it."
      ],
      "color": "#263749",
      "bgcolor": "#17232f"
    },
    {
      "id": 44,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "CAMERA INPUT \u00b7 source independent",
      "pos": [
        1440,
        30
      ],
      "size": [
        1120,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Motion includes its starting camera; a separate camera connection is optional.\nSaved jobs restores the edited camera as a sampled path. Original camera files and editable settings are retained in the local output directory.\nUploads expect individual animated actor files (GLB preferred) and an optional camera. Whole scenes with up to four actors and an embedded camera also work. Keep shared timing and world placement; GLB uses meters, Y-up.\nPerspective camera JSON can be imported into Blender with the helper included in the job ZIP. Fisheye paths remain supported in this viewer; the helper does not reproduce the fisheye shader."
      ],
      "color": "#263749",
      "bgcolor": "#17232f"
    },
